00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:09,025
- Hello, everyone.
- I see he was on <i>Society Game.</i>

231
00:10:09,108 --> 00:10:11,319
I'm Hyun Kyung-lyul,
and I currently work at Google.

232
00:10:11,402 --> 00:10:12,778
- A global corporation.
- That's right.

233
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:15,031
I also expected to see him here.

234
00:10:15,114 --> 00:10:17,867
<i>I couldn't find his account</i>
<i>to follow him on socials,</i>

235
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:19,952
but I definitely thought he'd be here.

236
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:22,830
I might end up going back
to my wife tonight at this rate.

237
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:24,540
I'm in serious trouble.

238
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:26,751
Sorry, but you should just leave today.

239
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:29,295
- I can't let that happen.
- Keep your car nearby.

240
00:10:29,378 --> 00:10:31,047
- Tell your manager to wait for you.
- Tell them to wait.

241
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:34,008
I told them to find a cheap place
to stay nearby.

242
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:36,010
Tell them to get two rooms.

243
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:38,220
- He'll also need a bed.
- Darn it.

244
00:10:39,764 --> 00:10:40,598
- Hello.
- What the heck?

245
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:43,517
Look who it is.

246
00:10:44,602 --> 00:10:45,519
It's John Park.

247
00:10:46,228 --> 00:10:48,648
Hello, I'm singer John Park.

248
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:51,400
<i>After graduating from</i>
<i>Northwestern University in the US</i>

249
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:52,902
<i>with a degree in economics,</i>

250
00:10:52,985 --> 00:10:56,822
<i>he debuted as a singer on </i>Superstar K
<i>and was the winner of </i>The Time Hotel.

251
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:59,909
<i>He is a fierce predator of survival shows.</i>

252
00:10:59,992 --> 00:11:02,078
- Hello.
- We even have the formidable John Park.

253
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:07,083
What are you even doing here?

254
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:08,042
What about you?

255
00:11:08,751 --> 00:11:09,919
Lots of surprises here.

256
00:11:11,128 --> 00:11:12,421
- Hello.
- Oh, hello!

257
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:15,424
- Oh, hello.
- That's Dong-jae.

258
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:18,302
I'm Kim Dong-jae,
a Season 1 contestant of <i>The Devil's Plan.</i>

259
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:20,513
<i>Kim Dong-jae left a lasting mark</i>

260
00:11:20,596 --> 00:11:25,142
<i>with his aggressive</i>
<i>and unorthodox gameplay in Season 1.</i>

261
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:28,187
<i>After becoming a world-class poker player,</i>

262
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:33,275
<i>he is back for another shot</i>
<i>at the title he never got to claim.</i>

263
00:11:33,859 --> 00:11:36,320
- Aren't we at 12 already?
- I'm like a newbie at the finals.

264
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:37,947
Did you talk to anyone from Season 1?

265
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:40,491
- Anyone say they'd be here?
- We have 12 already.

266
00:11:44,578 --> 00:11:46,664
- Hello, everyone! Salute!
- XITSUH!

267
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:49,583
My name is XITSUH,

268
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:53,671
and I was accepted into
Brigham Young University when I was 16.

269
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:57,633
<i>XITSUH has a remarkable academic history,</i>
<i>skipping grades in middle and high school</i>

270
00:11:57,717 --> 00:12:01,679
<i>and entering university early</i>
<i>while studying in the US.</i>

271
00:12:01,762 --> 00:12:05,015
<i>After proving his analytical mind</i>
<i>across multiple survival shows,</i>

272
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:08,686
<i>he now also works as a game designer.</i>

273
00:12:09,478 --> 00:12:11,105
He's known as "the survival game nutcase."

274
00:12:13,023 --> 00:12:14,525
- What's with everyone?
- It's gonna be intense.

275
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:16,569
We have really strong contestants.

276
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:17,653
This is gonna be fun.

277
00:12:17,737 --> 00:12:20,489
- The competition's insane.
- I feel like there will be one more.

278
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:21,782
There's more?

279
00:12:23,993 --> 00:12:26,287
- Hello.
- It's Yurisa.

280
00:12:26,370 --> 00:12:29,790
I'm Yurisa,
and I work as a subculture model,

281
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:32,835
YouTube singer, and poker player.

282
00:12:32,918 --> 00:12:35,713
<i>Yurisa is a high-intelligence powerhouse</i>
<i>recognized by Mensa,</i>

283
00:12:35,796 --> 00:12:39,675
<i>with an IQ of 156,</i>
<i>placing her in the top 1%.</i>

284
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:43,429
<i>Just six months into poker,</i>
<i>she won the Asian Ladies division,</i>

285
00:12:43,512 --> 00:12:45,890
<i>proving her ability beyond question.</i>

286
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:48,809
She's really shy,
so avoid talking to her if you can.

287
00:12:49,643 --> 00:12:50,644
- Have you been well?
- Yes.

288
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:53,355
Hold on, what about the former winners
of <i>The Devil's Plan</i>?

289
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:55,357
- There aren't any yet.
- They might come later.

290
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:57,610
It would make sense
if they came now to make 16.

291
00:12:57,693 --> 00:12:59,945
- No, that would be…
- Isn't it a given?

292
00:13:02,948 --> 00:13:04,074
I knew it!

293
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:06,202
I knew it!

294
00:13:06,285 --> 00:13:08,829
- You can't be serious.
- I guessed one right.

295
00:13:08,913 --> 00:13:10,331
- You guessed right.
- I knew it.

296
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:11,707
- What are you doing here?
- Of course.

297
00:13:11,791 --> 00:13:13,250
This is too much.

298
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:17,254
Hello, I'm Ha Seok-jin,
the winner of Season 1.

299
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:22,051
<i>Faced with a powerful alliance,</i>
<i>Ha Seok-jin claimed the ultimate victory</i>

300
00:13:22,134 --> 00:13:24,637
<i>through keen insight</i>
<i>and straightforward play in Season 1.</i>

301
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:30,184
<i>He is back to defend the honor</i>
<i>of being the inaugural champion.</i>

302
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:31,936
- It's nice to see you.
- Good to see you.

303
00:13:32,019 --> 00:13:34,355
- Just look at this cast.
- Hello.

304
00:13:34,438 --> 00:13:35,940
Seriously.

305
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:38,818
They really went all out this time.

306
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:40,736
Another one?

307
00:13:41,821 --> 00:13:43,239
- Seriously?
- They're all here.

308
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:45,533
- My goodness.
- They're all here.

309
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,576
- Hello.
- Hello.

310
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,579
- The winners from Season 1 and 2 are here.
- Why invite me to the grand final?

311
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:54,041
I'm Jeong Hyun-gyu, and I'm studying
physical education at SNU.

312
00:13:54,124 --> 00:13:56,502
I'm the winner
of <i>The Devil's Plan: Death Room.</i>

313
00:13:56,585 --> 00:14:00,631
<i>Jeong Hyun-gyu demonstrated</i>
<i>both ability and survival instinct</i>

314
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:04,176
<i>under extreme conditions</i>
<i>to win </i>The Devil's Plan: Death Room<i>.</i>

315
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:09,098
<i>He now sets out on a new journey</i>
<i>to prove himself once again.</i>

316
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:11,475
- Winners of Seasons 1 and 2.
- Hello.

317
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:12,726
The final winners.

318
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:14,395
Why would you invite the winners?

319
00:14:14,478 --> 00:14:16,647
- Yeah, now we're talking.
- Hello.

320
00:14:16,730 --> 00:14:18,649
- Stiff competition.
- This is gonna be fun.

321
00:14:19,316 --> 00:14:22,194
There are so many of us.
How's the elimination gonna go?

322
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:23,863
Two need to be eliminated per day.

323
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:25,990
Yeah, two per day,
since we're here for seven days.

324
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:28,701
If anyone has other plans,
feel free to just head out first.

325
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:32,246
Oh, there's the screen.

326
00:14:32,329 --> 00:14:33,706
<i>Hello.</i>

327
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:37,042
<i>I'd like to welcome you all</i>
<i>to </i>The Devil's Plan.

328
00:14:37,877 --> 00:14:42,131
<i>Over the next week, you will compete</i>
<i>in specially designed games</i>

329
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:44,592
<i>to identify the sharpest mind.</i>

330
00:14:44,675 --> 00:14:50,264
<i>Now, I will explain to you all</i>
<i>how these games will be conducted.</i>

331
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:55,060
<i>Everyone currently has one Piece</i>
<i>in their possession.</i>

332
00:14:55,644 --> 00:15:00,316
<i>Pieces will serve</i>
<i>as the central resource of the game,</i>

333
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:02,192
<i>and you can utilize them</i>
<i>to buy advantageous items</i>

334
00:15:02,276 --> 00:15:05,988
<i>or for leverage in player negotiations.</i>

335
00:15:06,071 --> 00:15:10,075
<i>The transfer of Pieces is permitted</i>
<i>only within the living space.</i>

336
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:14,246
<i>In this season of </i>The Devil's Plan<i>,</i>
<i>the number of Pieces a player holds</i>

337
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:16,665
<i>will not directly affect</i>
<i>their standing in the game.</i>

338
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:18,208
That's new.

339
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:21,962
<i>It will not be used to determine</i>
<i>your living space,</i>

340
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:25,132
<i>and even if you lose them all,</i>
<i>you will not be eliminated.</i>

341
00:15:25,215 --> 00:15:26,800
What? Then how are you eliminated?

342
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:31,430
<i>Players' fates will be decided</i>
<i>by the games alone.</i>

343
00:15:32,389 --> 00:15:36,018
- Nice.
<i>- Two games will be held every day.</i>

344
00:15:36,101 --> 00:15:37,102
Two games?

345
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:40,773
<i>The first game, the main match,</i>
<i>will be held during the day.</i>

346
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:44,318
<i>All surviving players</i>
<i>will participate in the main match,</i>

347
00:15:44,401 --> 00:15:47,905
<i>and the results of that game</i>
<i>will determine the players' fate.</i>

348
00:15:49,156 --> 00:15:51,992
<i>The lowest-ranking player</i>
<i>in the main match</i>

349
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:54,536
<i>will forfeit all their Pieces</i>

350
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:56,789
<i>and be eliminated from </i>The Devil's Plan.

351
00:15:56,872 --> 00:15:58,374
Eliminated immediately, huh?

352
00:15:58,457 --> 00:16:00,709
- Eliminated on the first day.
- In the main match?

353
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:02,670
- Gone.
- <i>Based on the main match rankings,</i>

354
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:05,589
<i>the top players will be assigned</i>
<i>to the living area,</i>

355
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:09,093
<i>and the bottom players</i>
<i>will be assigned to the prison.</i>

356
00:16:09,677 --> 00:16:11,804
- Split in half.
<i>- The players in prison</i>

357
00:16:11,887 --> 00:16:14,682
<i>will participate in the second game,</i>
<i>the prison match.</i>

358
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:15,933
Another elimination.

359
00:16:16,016 --> 00:16:17,393
It's the same as Season 2.

360
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:21,397
<i>The prison match will be conducted</i>
<i>with all the players in prison</i>

361
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:24,900
<i>and will result in at least</i>
<i>one player being eliminated.</i>

362
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:25,943
"At least one"?

363
00:16:26,026 --> 00:16:28,654
<i>The lowest-ranking player</i>
<i>in the prison match</i>

364
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:31,031
<i>will forfeit all their Pieces</i>

365
00:16:31,115 --> 00:16:33,659
<i>and be eliminated from </i>The Devil's Plan.

366
00:16:33,742 --> 00:16:35,661
- Oh dear.
- My goodness.

367
00:16:35,744 --> 00:16:41,291
<i>You will accomplish various missions</i>
<i>in the living and game areas</i>

368
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:44,003
<i>to gain prize tokens.</i>

369
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:47,840
<i>Every time a prize token is obtained,</i>

370
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:50,509
<i>the prize money will increase</i>
<i>by 100 million won.</i>

371
00:16:51,427 --> 00:16:55,806
<i>You will have the chance</i>
<i>to obtain five tokens in total</i>

372
00:16:55,889 --> 00:17:00,144
<i>and, in turn, a chance to create</i>
<i>a prize pool of 500 million won.</i>

373
00:17:00,227 --> 00:17:01,145
Let's go for it.

374
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:05,232
<i>Violence and theft</i>
<i>are strictly prohibited.</i>

375
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:07,526
<i>Please keep that in mind.</i>

376
00:17:07,609 --> 00:17:08,902
So we can't do anything.

377
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:12,406
- <i>Before we begin our first main match,</i>
- You think you can?

378
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:14,950
<i>you may spend your free time as you wish.</i>

379
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:17,286
Eliminating someone after the main match?

380
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:19,079
- Yeah.
- That's rough.

381
00:17:19,163 --> 00:17:20,289
- I don't wanna go.
- Right?

382
00:17:20,372 --> 00:17:23,042
<i>The second you lose focus,</i>
<i>you could be eliminated.</i>

383
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:24,376
You have a 1 out of 16 chance.

384
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:27,087
<i>I was actually glad to hear that.</i>

385
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:29,673
If I do well in the main match,
I don't have to worry

386
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:31,425
about retaliation
if another player is eliminated.

387
00:17:31,508 --> 00:17:34,261
Then I can betray them without worrying.

388
00:17:34,344 --> 00:17:37,431
<i>Up until now, you were guaranteed</i>
<i>a second chance in the game.</i>

389
00:17:37,514 --> 00:17:40,559
But now, a single well-aimed blow
could be fatal.

390
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:42,269
You have to do well in every game.

391
00:17:42,352 --> 00:17:44,855
Even one mistake can be your downfall.

392
00:17:44,938 --> 00:17:45,981
Dong-min.

393
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:48,233
- Gosh.
- It's nice to see you again.

394
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:50,402
I'm sure you'll deliver again.

395
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:51,737
You always do.

396
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:57,117
- Come on now.
- Hello.

397
00:17:57,201 --> 00:17:59,286
- What's going on here?
- No, it's not what you think.

398
00:17:59,369 --> 00:18:01,663
- What's up?
- This room is nice.

399
00:18:01,747 --> 00:18:04,041
I actually just rewatched
<i>The Genius </i>recently.

400
00:18:04,124 --> 00:18:05,959
- Thank you.
- Whenever you two

401
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:08,545
gathered like this in the early stages,
things happened.

402
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:10,005
No, that's not true.

403
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,507
I'm just saying hi to everyone.

404
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:12,591
- Are you?
- Yeah.

405
00:18:12,674 --> 00:18:15,719
<i>Jang Dong-min and Oh Hyun-min</i>
<i>are the most iconic duo in the history</i>

406
00:18:15,803 --> 00:18:17,387
<i>of the brain survival genre.</i>

407
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:21,475
<i>The so-called Jang-Oh Alliance</i>
<i>proved powerful enough to secure spots</i>

408
00:18:21,558 --> 00:18:23,644
<i>for both players in the finals.</i>

409
00:18:23,727 --> 00:18:24,770
There's Jang-Oh.

410
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:26,939
- Hello.
- Hello.

411
00:18:27,022 --> 00:18:28,524
- Are you having a secret meeting?
- What?

412
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:29,900
- Is this a secret meeting?
- I'm gonna take a spin.

413
00:18:29,983 --> 00:18:31,318
- Sure, go ahead.
- Hello.

414
00:18:31,401 --> 00:18:32,444
Hello.

415
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:34,863
Please allow me to join Jang-Oh.

416
00:18:37,324 --> 00:18:39,743
I'd be so honored to be a part of Jang-Oh.

417
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:42,913
<i>It's the inevitable nature of survival.</i>

418
00:18:42,996 --> 00:18:47,000
People naturally find themselves
drawn to the strong.

419
00:18:47,084 --> 00:18:48,001
It's almost instinct.

420
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:50,337
<i>I think the two major alliances</i>
<i>will be led by Jang Dong-min</i>

421
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,880
<i>and Hong Jin-ho.</i>

422
00:18:51,964 --> 00:18:58,345
And I think taking those two out first
would be best for us.

423
00:18:58,428 --> 00:19:00,222
So, where do you work now?

424
00:19:00,305 --> 00:19:01,140
I work at LG Uplus.

425
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:03,058
Really? Oh wow.

426
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:04,560
You work at a nice company.

427
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:05,686
I hope we get along.

428
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:07,729
- Sure.
- Seriously though.

429
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:09,314
- There are so many amazing players.
- Right?

430
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:11,525
They're all serious competition.

431
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:13,068
- But you know what?
- What?

432
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:15,487
When there are a lot of leaders around,

433
00:19:15,571 --> 00:19:18,365
choosing a second-in-command
is where it gets most competitive.

434
00:19:18,448 --> 00:19:21,368
- Right.
- Finding someone you can trust.

435
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:24,037
A few here clearly aren't the type
to answer to anyone.

436
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:24,955
You're right.

437
00:19:25,038 --> 00:19:27,332
- Alliances will form.
- Different factions.

438
00:19:27,416 --> 00:19:30,002
If it's set up to eliminate someone
during the main match,

439
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:31,753
it's a game of politics at the end.

440
00:19:32,462 --> 00:19:34,256
I've done my share of survival games,

441
00:19:34,339 --> 00:19:35,632
so I know where I excel.

442
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:36,675
And it's not at the top.

443
00:19:36,758 --> 00:19:38,218
I can't be a leader.

444
00:19:38,302 --> 00:19:41,889
<i>There's Jin-ho,</i>
<i>with whom I've been on a team before.</i>

445
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:45,267
<i>I've briefly been on the same team</i>
<i>as Dong-min,</i>

446
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:47,352
<i>and I've also faced him as an opponent.</i>

447
00:19:47,436 --> 00:19:49,897
<i>Obviously, we also have Ha Seok-jin</i>

448
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:50,856
<i>and Jeong Hyun-gyu.</i>

449
00:19:50,939 --> 00:19:54,318
<i>This is their home ground.</i>
<i>They've already won once here.</i>

450
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:58,030
<i>So I consider them to be</i>
<i>on that leader level.</i>

451
00:19:58,113 --> 00:20:01,825
I think I could have great synergy
with any of them.

452
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:04,369
- It hasn't sunk in yet.
- I know.

453
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:08,040
- I feel like I'm just visiting a set.
- Just to hang out.

454
00:20:08,123 --> 00:20:10,709
But once we start getting into it

455
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:12,544
- and people start being eliminated…
- Tearing each other apart.

456
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:15,088
We'll probably be crying
and cursing each other out, right?

457
00:20:15,172 --> 00:20:17,633
- You two are already stuck at the hip.
- I know, right?

458
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:19,301
What's so wrong about that?

459
00:20:20,093 --> 00:20:22,012
- Why can't we be? We're friends.
- He's right.

460
00:20:22,095 --> 00:20:24,348
Don't whisper
and screw yourself over again.

461
00:20:24,431 --> 00:20:25,390
No whispering this time.

462
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:26,975
I'll speak loudly this time.

463
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:28,936
"Everything going well over there?"
Like that.

464
00:20:29,019 --> 00:20:30,312
Dong-jae, are you looking to win?

465
00:20:30,395 --> 00:20:32,064
- Of course.
- That's the spirit.

466
00:20:32,147 --> 00:20:34,024
- I came to win.
- I've been waiting to hear that.

467
00:20:34,107 --> 00:20:36,068
- Hello, I'm Yi Do.
- Oh, hello.

468
00:20:36,151 --> 00:20:37,402
- We're alumni.
- Oh, I see.

469
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:38,445
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

470
00:20:38,528 --> 00:20:39,446
I'm Jeong Hyun-gyu.

471
00:20:39,529 --> 00:20:41,865
- Of course, I know who you are.
- Right.

472
00:20:41,949 --> 00:20:44,701
I see you're back again,
though you already won.

473
00:20:44,785 --> 00:20:46,912
I guess I haven't
gotten it out of my system.

474
00:20:46,995 --> 00:20:50,374
<i>I've had the same mindset since Season 2.</i>

475
00:20:50,457 --> 00:20:51,875
I wanna win it all.

476
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:53,418
That's why I'm here.

477
00:20:56,171 --> 00:20:58,632
He walks in there
like a chairman entering his office.

478
00:20:58,715 --> 00:20:59,967
He expects people to come to him.

479
00:21:02,678 --> 00:21:05,055
I should go and check it out.

480
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:07,766
- He's calling you up.
- Let me sneak up there first.

481
00:21:07,849 --> 00:21:09,726
I wonder who will come up.

482
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:11,645
Let them come to you.

483
00:21:11,728 --> 00:21:13,313
There he is.

484
00:21:14,147 --> 00:21:15,857
- Chairman.
- Yes, hello.

485
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:23,115
Getting a read on personalities
is also important.

486
00:21:23,198 --> 00:21:26,910
Right now, you might think
no one here is capable of betrayal.

487
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:29,162
But you need to figure out
who's hungry for power.

488
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:33,542
- From what I see, that salaryman.
- Yeah.

489
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:35,335
- The LG guy?
- Yeah.

490
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:37,170
I think he possesses that quality.

491
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:39,214
- You can see that?
- Yeah.

492
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:40,966
He has that side to him.

493
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:45,345
And that guy, Hyun Kyung-lyul,

494
00:21:46,471 --> 00:21:48,515
is competitive.

495
00:21:48,598 --> 00:21:52,894
So, it might not come naturally to him,
but he will turn to that if needed.

496
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:54,396
- Right.
- Yeah.

497
00:21:57,190 --> 00:21:58,734
- So…
- So we'll join forces?

498
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:00,610
Yeah, let's keep the door open for that,

499
00:22:00,694 --> 00:22:02,863
- but you should have your people lined up.
- Of course.

500
00:22:07,993 --> 00:22:09,870
- Oh gosh.
- Hey, XITSUH.

501
00:22:09,953 --> 00:22:11,747
- Dong-min.
- My goodness.

502
00:22:11,830 --> 00:22:12,914
Is this the reception room?

503
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:15,709
- Oh, well…
- Is this where you repent your sins?

504
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:17,794
It's my private office.

505
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:20,172
- You already got yourself an office?
- Yeah.

506
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:24,134
I was surprised to hear
there will be no death game.

507
00:22:24,217 --> 00:22:26,928
I'm sure our skills
will decide our rankings.

508
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:30,599
But let's say 11 or 12 people team up.

509
00:22:30,682 --> 00:22:34,811
Large groups like that will be risky.
They crumble in an instant.

510
00:22:34,895 --> 00:22:36,938
That's true.
Only half will be in the living area.

511
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:38,065
Right.

512
00:22:38,148 --> 00:22:39,941
You don't need to worry about that.

513
00:22:40,025 --> 00:22:42,152
Honestly, it would be a blessing
if that happens.

514
00:22:42,235 --> 00:22:43,945
It's much easier to break them apart.

515
00:22:45,447 --> 00:22:48,492
All right, XITSUH.
I'll be considering you an ally.

516
00:22:48,575 --> 00:22:51,036
Sure thing.
I'm here for you if you need me.

517
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:54,915
It's time.

518
00:22:54,998 --> 00:22:56,792
<i>The time is up.</i>

519
00:22:56,875 --> 00:22:59,211
<i>Everyone, please gather in the hall.</i>

520
00:22:59,836 --> 00:23:00,837
There they are.

521
00:23:03,298 --> 00:23:04,591
The top celebrities.

522
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:09,721
- It's been a while.
- Nice to meet you.

523
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:11,932
Goodness. Hello.

524
00:23:12,015 --> 00:23:15,727
<i>Now, let me introduce</i>
<i>the first main match.</i>

525
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:18,397
<i>The first main match</i>
<i>of </i>The Devil's Plan <i>is</i>

526
00:23:19,272 --> 00:23:20,941
<i>Either Or.</i>

527
00:23:21,024 --> 00:23:22,150
- Come on.
- What's that?

528
00:23:22,234 --> 00:23:26,113
<i>In Either Or,</i>
<i>players will choose between two options</i>

529
00:23:26,196 --> 00:23:29,074
<i>to gain as many points as possible.</i>

530
00:23:29,157 --> 00:23:30,742
So it's based on points.

531
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:34,162
<i>Players will make</i>
<i>a total of ten selections</i>

532
00:23:34,246 --> 00:23:36,248
<i>and play four mini-games.</i>

533
00:23:36,998 --> 00:23:41,545
<i>The options and rules of the mini-games</i>
<i>will not be disclosed beforehand.</i>

534
00:23:42,045 --> 00:23:45,173
<i>They will be revealed one by one</i>
<i>as the game unfolds.</i>

535
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:48,218
<i>Throughout the game,</i>

536
00:23:48,301 --> 00:23:51,179
<i>players will check their options</i>
<i>as they appear</i>

537
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:55,016
<i>and make their selections</i>
<i>using the provided devices.</i>

538
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:59,604
<i>Players will gain points</i>
<i>based on the selections they make</i>

539
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:01,481
<i>and the results of the mini-game.</i>

540
00:24:01,565 --> 00:24:03,400
<i>Any change in points</i>

541
00:24:03,483 --> 00:24:06,236
<i>will trigger a reveal of all players'</i>
<i>cumulative scores.</i>

542
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:09,531
<i>The game will end</i>
<i>when all the selections are made</i>

543
00:24:09,614 --> 00:24:11,074
<i>and the mini-games conclude.</i>

544
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:14,494
<i>The final rankings will determine</i>
<i>the players' accommodations.</i>

545
00:24:15,328 --> 00:24:18,665
<i>Two players will be eliminated</i>
<i>in this main match.</i>

546
00:24:18,748 --> 00:24:20,000
- Two?
- No way.

547
00:24:20,083 --> 00:24:21,585
Two eliminations?

548
00:24:22,085 --> 00:24:24,337
<i>Players in first through sixth place</i>
<i>will go to the living area,</i>

549
00:24:24,421 --> 00:24:27,924
<i>and players in seventh through fourteenth</i>
<i>will go to prison.</i>

550
00:24:28,008 --> 00:24:30,635
<i>The bottom two players will be eliminated.</i>

551
00:24:30,719 --> 00:24:31,636
That's brutal.

552
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,722
<i>The top-ranking player</i>

553
00:24:33,805 --> 00:24:35,599
<i>will be rewarded with an advantage,</i>

554
00:24:35,682 --> 00:24:37,767
<i>the alliance token.</i>

555
00:24:37,851 --> 00:24:38,685
What?

556
00:24:38,768 --> 00:24:39,853
<i>The alliance token</i>

557
00:24:39,936 --> 00:24:42,397
<i>will allow the first-place player</i>

558
00:24:42,481 --> 00:24:46,610
<i>to select a player bound for prison</i>
<i>and bring them to the living area.</i>

559
00:24:48,487 --> 00:24:53,116
<i>Please use</i>
<i>the alliance token strategically.</i>

560
00:24:53,617 --> 00:24:56,870
<i>The devices will now be handed out.</i>

561
00:24:58,455 --> 00:24:59,664
State-of-the-art stuff.

562
00:24:59,748 --> 00:25:00,957
- Nucksal.
- Thank you.

563
00:25:01,458 --> 00:25:03,835
They have privacy screen protectors
on them.

564
00:25:05,253 --> 00:25:08,590
<i>We will now begin the first selection.</i>

565
00:25:08,673 --> 00:25:09,925
- Already?
- Just like that?

566
00:25:10,008 --> 00:25:11,510
- We're starting?
- Just like this?

567
00:25:11,593 --> 00:25:13,678
<i>Players who choose the performance bonus</i>

568
00:25:13,762 --> 00:25:18,934
<i>will receive one Piece</i>
<i>if they end up in the living area.</i>

569
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:21,770
<i>Players who choose the insurance payout</i>

570
00:25:21,853 --> 00:25:25,607
<i>will receive two Pieces</i>
<i>if they end up in prison.</i>

571
00:25:25,690 --> 00:25:27,150
PERFORMANCE BONUS / INSURANCE PAYOUT

572
00:25:27,234 --> 00:25:28,485
That's fun.

573
00:25:28,568 --> 00:25:32,697
<i>Now, please choose either</i>
<i>the performance bonus or insurance payout</i>

574
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:34,991
<i>using the devices.</i>

575
00:25:35,075 --> 00:25:37,744
So it all depends on where you end up.

576
00:25:37,827 --> 00:25:40,664
This is basically
asking you to predict your outcome.

577
00:25:40,747 --> 00:25:41,623
You're right.

578
00:25:41,706 --> 00:25:43,875
I don't think I can play
in the living area.

579
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:46,169
Then you have to go for option two.

580
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:47,921
I just chose the one with better odds.

581
00:25:48,004 --> 00:25:49,881
I chose prison.

582
00:25:49,965 --> 00:25:51,800
Who knows what might happen in prison?

583
00:25:51,883 --> 00:25:53,885
There might be a mission
where you need a Piece,

584
00:25:53,969 --> 00:25:56,304
or Pieces could be used against players.

585
00:25:56,388 --> 00:25:57,764
<i>I'm not saying going to prison is my goal.</i>

586
00:25:57,847 --> 00:26:00,100
<i>But if I do end up there,</i>
<i>I wanna be armed.</i>

587
00:26:00,183 --> 00:26:01,309
What are you choosing?

588
00:26:01,935 --> 00:26:03,603
- I'm gonna choose option one.
- Yeah?

589
00:26:03,687 --> 00:26:05,730
Yeah, going to the living area
should be the goal.

590
00:26:05,814 --> 00:26:07,482
<i>When it comes to survival,</i>

591
00:26:07,566 --> 00:26:11,861
I think you should avoid situations
where you're backed into a corner.

592
00:26:11,945 --> 00:26:13,863
I also thought choosing option one

593
00:26:13,947 --> 00:26:17,117
would encourage me to play even harder
to avoid ending up in prison.

594
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:19,119
It's like a stick I'm holding over myself.

595
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:20,870
Which one did you choose?

596
00:26:20,954 --> 00:26:21,830
I chose two.

597
00:26:21,913 --> 00:26:22,914
- Really?
- Yeah.

598
00:26:22,998 --> 00:26:23,915
Why?

599
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:26,209
- For insurance, just in case.
- I see.

600
00:26:26,918 --> 00:26:29,170
- I chose one.
- I did too.

601
00:26:30,088 --> 00:26:31,715
- All right, I'm done.
- Me too.

602
00:26:31,798 --> 00:26:34,092
I just have to trust my gut.

603
00:26:34,175 --> 00:26:37,220
<i>All players</i>
<i>have completed their selections.</i>

604
00:26:37,304 --> 00:26:39,598
SELECTION 1
PERFORMANCE BONUS / INSURANCE PAYOUT

605
00:26:39,681 --> 00:26:42,934
<i>The first mini-game will now be revealed.</i>

606
00:26:43,435 --> 00:26:47,564
<i>This mini-game</i>
<i>will determine the priority ranking</i>

607
00:26:47,647 --> 00:26:50,025
<i>in all tie situations going forward.</i>

608
00:26:52,986 --> 00:26:55,280
<i>The first mini-game of Either Or is</i>

609
00:26:55,363 --> 00:26:56,615
<i>Count the Cubes.</i>

610
00:26:57,282 --> 00:26:59,784
<i>In Count the Cubes,</i>
<i>players will have to figure out</i>

611
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:02,495
<i>the number of cubes</i>
<i>based on the given diagram.</i>

612
00:27:02,579 --> 00:27:03,997
So we'll use this to answer it.

613
00:27:04,080 --> 00:27:05,373
<i>Once the diagram is revealed,</i>

614
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:08,376
<i>the players must confirm</i>
<i>the number of cubes</i>

615
00:27:08,460 --> 00:27:12,922
<i>and enter the answer on their devices.</i>

616
00:27:13,006 --> 00:27:16,635
<i>Answers may only be submitted</i>
<i>using the device.</i>

617
00:27:16,718 --> 00:27:18,136
<i>Once their answer is entered,</i>

618
00:27:18,219 --> 00:27:21,514
<i>the dealer will confirm</i>
<i>whether or not it is correct.</i>

619
00:27:21,598 --> 00:27:23,767
<i>If the answer they submitted is incorrect,</i>

620
00:27:23,850 --> 00:27:26,645
<i>the player will not be able to submit</i>
<i>another one for 20 seconds.</i>

621
00:27:26,728 --> 00:27:27,562
That's nuts.

622
00:27:27,646 --> 00:27:31,441
<i>The game will conclude</i>
<i>once 15 players answer correctly.</i>

623
00:27:31,524 --> 00:27:34,569
<i>The players will be ranked</i>
<i>according to the order</i>

624
00:27:34,653 --> 00:27:36,363
<i>in which they answered correctly.</i>

625
00:27:36,446 --> 00:27:39,824
- So first-come, first-served?
<i>- The high-ranked players of this mini-game</i>

626
00:27:39,908 --> 00:27:42,494
<i>will be given an advantage</i>

627
00:27:42,577 --> 00:27:47,499
<i>if a tie occurs</i>
<i>in any future mini-game of Either Or.</i>

628
00:27:47,582 --> 00:27:50,877
- Priority over anyone you tie with.
- The order… I see.

629
00:27:50,960 --> 00:27:53,046
<i>I don't think this priority ranking</i>

630
00:27:53,129 --> 00:27:55,757
will only come into play
when there's a tie.

631
00:27:55,840 --> 00:27:59,678
<i>I thought that it might actually</i>
<i>be the key to the whole match.</i>

632
00:27:59,761 --> 00:28:02,639
They said this priority ranking
will affect you until the end,

633
00:28:02,722 --> 00:28:06,685
so doing my best
to get a high ranking first would be best.

634
00:28:06,768 --> 00:28:08,895
You're good at stuff like this,
aren't you?

635
00:28:08,978 --> 00:28:09,896
- Sorry?
- This is your forte.

636
00:28:11,147 --> 00:28:12,982
<i>I love math.</i>

637
00:28:13,066 --> 00:28:17,904
Math was the one subject in school
that I worked really hard at.

638
00:28:17,987 --> 00:28:19,406
I wonder how difficult they'll be.

639
00:28:19,489 --> 00:28:20,407
Maybe like 20 diagrams?

640
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:22,659
You think 20 will be enough
to determine a winner?

641
00:28:22,742 --> 00:28:24,035
I mean, it's about speed.

642
00:28:26,955 --> 00:28:30,959
<i>Count the Cubes will now begin.</i>

643
00:28:31,543 --> 00:28:33,378
<i>Here is the first diagram.</i>

644
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:36,840
- What the heck?
- Seriously?

645
00:28:39,342 --> 00:28:41,052
I guess I have to write it down.

646
00:28:48,601 --> 00:28:50,061
This is way too hard.

647
00:28:53,606 --> 00:28:54,774
Man, I have no clue.

648
00:28:58,695 --> 00:29:00,196
JUNG WON-YOUNG: 336

649
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:01,823
Jung Won-young, incorrect.

650
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:19,007
Kim Dong-jae,

651
00:29:20,133 --> 00:29:21,092
correct.

652
00:29:21,885 --> 00:29:23,011
Damn it.

653
00:29:23,636 --> 00:29:25,346
JUNG WON-YOUNG: 360

654
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:27,056
Jung Won-young, correct.

655
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:28,683
PRIORITY RANKING

656
00:29:28,767 --> 00:29:30,894
The moment the diagram appeared,

657
00:29:30,977 --> 00:29:33,188
I entered my answer, certain I'd be first.

658
00:29:33,271 --> 00:29:35,190
<i>That 20-second penalty was such a waste.</i>

659
00:29:35,273 --> 00:29:37,901
<i>I'm frustrated</i>
<i>that I lost first place to Dong-jae.</i>

660
00:29:38,526 --> 00:29:40,195
Hyun Kyung-lyul, correct.

661
00:29:40,278 --> 00:29:41,780
Jeong Hyun-gyu, correct.

662
00:29:41,863 --> 00:29:43,448
Ha Seok-jin, correct.

663
00:29:43,531 --> 00:29:45,784
As expected of us. Well done.

664
00:29:45,867 --> 00:29:48,703
XITSUH, Oh Hyun-min, and Stella Jang.
All correct.

665
00:29:48,787 --> 00:29:50,330
John Park, correct.

666
00:29:52,290 --> 00:29:53,583
I took too long.

667
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:06,638
I expected a lot more
from Dong-min and Jin-ho.

668
00:30:10,433 --> 00:30:12,018
Jang Dong-min, correct.

669
00:30:13,561 --> 00:30:15,355
Yi Do, correct.

670
00:30:15,438 --> 00:30:16,940
Yurisa, correct.

671
00:30:17,023 --> 00:30:18,441
Nucksal, correct.

672
00:30:18,525 --> 00:30:19,567
Nice.

673
00:30:29,494 --> 00:30:31,204
- You got it, right?
- Not yet.

674
00:30:33,790 --> 00:30:36,251
Add up all the numbers
and write down your total first.

675
00:30:39,879 --> 00:30:41,339
It's much higher than that.

676
00:30:42,549 --> 00:30:43,383
Really?

677
00:30:44,008 --> 00:30:47,303
Write down your total, and I'll tell you
if you need to go higher or lower.

678
00:30:47,387 --> 00:30:48,388
Okay.

679
00:30:49,222 --> 00:30:50,974
I want you to stay.

680
00:30:52,308 --> 00:30:53,142
Down.

681
00:30:54,561 --> 00:30:55,395
Up.

682
00:31:03,820 --> 00:31:05,488
Shindong, correct.

683
00:31:09,158 --> 00:31:10,201
I think I got it.

684
00:31:10,910 --> 00:31:12,203
Hong Jin-ho, incorrect.

685
00:31:12,287 --> 00:31:13,413
Seriously?

686
00:31:13,496 --> 00:31:14,789
JAE JAE, incorrect.

687
00:31:14,873 --> 00:31:16,583
Darn it. Seriously?

688
00:31:17,250 --> 00:31:19,752
<i>I first divided it into sections</i>
<i>before counting.</i>

689
00:31:19,836 --> 00:31:22,005
The bottom level was ten by ten,

690
00:31:22,088 --> 00:31:24,299
<i>and there were two levels of that.</i>

691
00:31:24,382 --> 00:31:28,511
<i>Then, the 2-4-6-8 sections</i>
<i>each had 20 cubes total,</i>

692
00:31:28,595 --> 00:31:30,054
<i>and there were four levels of those.</i>

693
00:31:30,138 --> 00:31:33,474
<i>And then, the ten-ten diagonal cross.</i>

694
00:31:33,558 --> 00:31:35,351
<i>There were four levels of those.</i>

695
00:31:35,435 --> 00:31:37,770
<i>If you add them all up, you get 360.</i>

696
00:31:37,854 --> 00:31:38,938
I think I did well.

697
00:31:39,022 --> 00:31:40,648
Hong Jin-ho, correct.

698
00:31:40,732 --> 00:31:42,901
I'm an idiot.
I really messed up the calculations.

699
00:31:42,984 --> 00:31:44,235
- Unbelievable.
- Wait.

700
00:31:44,319 --> 00:31:47,447
- <i>Fifteen players have answered correctly.</i>
<i>- </i>Damn it.

701
00:31:47,530 --> 00:31:49,365
- It's over.
- <i>That concludes the game.</i>

702
00:31:49,449 --> 00:31:52,744
<i>Here are the results</i>
<i>of the first mini-game.</i>

703
00:31:52,827 --> 00:31:53,661
First!

704
00:31:53,745 --> 00:31:55,830
- I should've chosen option two earlier.
- I'm last.

705
00:31:55,914 --> 00:31:59,000
<i>Should a tie in score occur going forward,</i>

706
00:31:59,083 --> 00:32:02,337
<i>the ranking will be settled</i>
<i>by this priority ranking.</i>

707
00:32:03,630 --> 00:32:06,591
<i>The second mini-game will now be revealed.</i>

708
00:32:06,674 --> 00:32:07,842
- What?
- Already?

709
00:32:07,926 --> 00:32:09,969
<i>The second mini-game of Either Or is</i>

710
00:32:10,053 --> 00:32:11,346
<i>Count the Rectangles.</i>

711
00:32:11,429 --> 00:32:13,556
Again? Let's stop counting already.
My eyes hurt.

712
00:32:13,640 --> 00:32:15,141
We <i>just </i>counted cubes.

713
00:32:15,224 --> 00:32:16,935
- My eyes are burning.
- Enough already.

714
00:32:17,018 --> 00:32:18,978
<i>In Count the Rectangles,</i>
<i>players must determine</i>

715
00:32:19,062 --> 00:32:21,606
<i>the number of rectangles</i>
<i>that can be formed on the game board</i>

716
00:32:21,689 --> 00:32:23,524
<i>to reach the target number.</i>

717
00:32:23,608 --> 00:32:25,443
<i>Before the game begins,</i>

718
00:32:25,526 --> 00:32:28,529
<i>players may form teams</i>
<i>with whoever they wish.</i>

719
00:32:28,613 --> 00:32:31,115
<i>Each team must have three players,</i>

720
00:32:31,199 --> 00:32:32,909
<i>and once a team is formed,</i>

721
00:32:32,992 --> 00:32:36,245
<i>it cannot be canceled or changed</i>
<i>until the end of the game.</i>

722
00:32:36,329 --> 00:32:37,789
<i>Once the game begins,</i>

723
00:32:37,872 --> 00:32:40,625
<i>the game board and target number</i>
<i>will be revealed.</i>

724
00:32:40,708 --> 00:32:44,921
<i>The game board</i>
<i>will be made up of multiple square cells,</i>

725
00:32:45,004 --> 00:32:47,799
<i>and some of them will contain numbers.</i>

726
00:32:47,882 --> 00:32:49,300
<i>Once the board is revealed,</i>

727
00:32:49,384 --> 00:32:52,720
<i>players must figure out</i>
<i>how many rectangular formations</i>

728
00:32:52,804 --> 00:32:57,058
<i>reach the target number</i>
<i>when their numbers are added up.</i>

729
00:32:58,059 --> 00:33:00,728
<i>Once a player determines</i>
<i>the total number of rectangles,</i>

730
00:33:00,812 --> 00:33:04,190
<i>they can press the buzzer</i>
<i>and give their answer within ten seconds.</i>

731
00:33:04,273 --> 00:33:06,109
<i>If the answer is incorrect,</i>

732
00:33:06,192 --> 00:33:11,280
<i>the player's team cannot attempt</i>
<i>the same question again.</i>

733
00:33:11,364 --> 00:33:12,532
So just one chance?

734
00:33:12,615 --> 00:33:15,618
<i>The first team to get two correct answers</i>
<i>will become the winning team</i>

735
00:33:15,702 --> 00:33:18,246
<i>and be exempt from the rest of the game.</i>

736
00:33:19,205 --> 00:33:22,125
<i>There will be a five-minute time limit</i>
<i>for every question.</i>

737
00:33:22,208 --> 00:33:25,628
<i>If there is no team that gets</i>
<i>the correct answer within the time limit</i>

738
00:33:25,712 --> 00:33:28,006
<i>or if all teams give an incorrect answer,</i>

739
00:33:28,089 --> 00:33:29,757
<i>the next question will be presented.</i>

740
00:33:30,508 --> 00:33:34,804
<i>The game will conclude</i>
<i>once half the teams become winning teams.</i>

741
00:33:35,346 --> 00:33:37,432
- I have to win this.
- <i>Each winning team</i>

742
00:33:37,515 --> 00:33:39,475
<i>will split seven points among its members,</i>

743
00:33:40,143 --> 00:33:41,269
<i>and each losing team</i>

744
00:33:41,352 --> 00:33:44,230
<i>will share a penalty of up to -4 points</i>
<i>among themselves.</i>

745
00:33:44,313 --> 00:33:45,148
"Up to"?

746
00:33:45,231 --> 00:33:46,983
<i>Before the game,</i>

747
00:33:47,066 --> 00:33:49,485
<i>we will begin the second selection.</i>

748
00:33:50,737 --> 00:33:52,947
EITHER OR SELECTION 2
TEAM / INDIVIDUAL

749
00:33:53,031 --> 00:33:58,036
<i>Players will choose to either play</i>
<i>as a team of three or as an individual</i>

750
00:33:58,119 --> 00:34:00,538
<i>and inform the dealer.</i>

751
00:34:00,621 --> 00:34:04,917
<i>Individual players</i>
<i>will earn seven points upon winning.</i>

752
00:34:05,001 --> 00:34:07,962
<i>If they lose, they will lose three points.</i>

753
00:34:08,588 --> 00:34:12,800
So if you play solo and lose,
you take the full -4 points alone.

754
00:34:12,884 --> 00:34:15,219
- Only -3 for solo.
- Oh, -3 points?

755
00:34:15,303 --> 00:34:17,388
Playing solo will be
high-risk, high-return.

756
00:34:17,472 --> 00:34:20,141
I think playing solo
is out of the question for me.

757
00:34:20,224 --> 00:34:21,726
I think teams would be better.

758
00:34:23,311 --> 00:34:25,021
The three of us will play as a team.

759
00:34:25,104 --> 00:34:26,773
- The three of you on one team?
- Yes.

760
00:34:26,856 --> 00:34:29,275
Kim Dong-jae, Oh Hyun-min,
and Jung Won-young,

761
00:34:29,358 --> 00:34:30,276
you are now a team.

762
00:34:30,359 --> 00:34:31,611
Look at that trio.

763
00:34:31,694 --> 00:34:34,363
- The brains have teamed up.
- Top-tier team.

764
00:34:34,447 --> 00:34:37,033
I actually thought Hyun-min
would come to me,

765
00:34:37,867 --> 00:34:39,952
but he joined forces
with the first and second-place guys,

766
00:34:40,036 --> 00:34:42,080
<i>without approaching me at all.</i>

767
00:34:43,372 --> 00:34:44,207
Darn it.

768
00:34:44,916 --> 00:34:46,918
I mean, this is…

769
00:34:47,001 --> 00:34:50,379
As soon as teams were mentioned,
Hyun-min came to me.

770
00:34:50,463 --> 00:34:51,839
Join me and Dong-jae.

771
00:34:52,715 --> 00:34:55,301
A team of the top three players?
Sounds good to me.

772
00:34:55,384 --> 00:34:56,260
Truth is…

773
00:34:56,344 --> 00:34:57,887
OH HYUN-MIN

774
00:34:57,970 --> 00:34:59,180
…I know what I bring.

775
00:34:59,263 --> 00:35:01,766
My biggest merit

776
00:35:01,849 --> 00:35:06,729
is this image that I've built
that makes people think I'm good at games.

777
00:35:06,813 --> 00:35:11,359
<i>Would anyone turn me down</i>
<i>if I approached them to team up?</i>

778
00:35:11,442 --> 00:35:13,694
I was certain they wouldn't.

779
00:35:13,778 --> 00:35:19,742
So I decided I need to build a solid team
with whoever's leading and take the win.

780
00:35:19,826 --> 00:35:21,369
Please choose a team name.

781
00:35:21,452 --> 00:35:22,745
- Rectangle?
- "Rectangle"?

782
00:35:22,829 --> 00:35:24,455
- Team Rectangle.
- I like that. Let's go with that.

783
00:35:24,539 --> 00:35:26,582
- You are Team Rectangle.
- Thank you.

784
00:35:26,666 --> 00:35:27,834
A team of aces.

785
00:35:27,917 --> 00:35:29,627
- They're so quick.
- Such a strong team.

786
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:31,212
Are you going solo?

787
00:35:31,295 --> 00:35:33,256
- Maybe a team?
- Should we team up?

788
00:35:33,339 --> 00:35:34,507
- Team up?
- Sure.

789
00:35:34,590 --> 00:35:37,009
<i>In terms of building rapport</i>
<i>with the other players,</i>

790
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:40,596
I figured it wouldn't hurt to team up
since this isn't a high-stakes game.

791
00:35:40,680 --> 00:35:41,639
Join us, John.

792
00:35:41,722 --> 00:35:42,557
Join you two?

793
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:45,101
- We might as well give it a go.
- Yeah, why not?

794
00:35:45,184 --> 00:35:47,061
- There's no risk yet.
- Right.

795
00:35:47,145 --> 00:35:48,354
- We'll be a team.
- Us three.

796
00:35:48,437 --> 00:35:49,480
Please choose a team name.

797
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:51,774
- Gomoku.
- You're not good at that game though.

798
00:35:51,858 --> 00:35:53,109
- Team Gomoku?
- Yes.

799
00:35:53,192 --> 00:35:55,570
- You are Team Gomoku.
- Great.

800
00:35:56,070 --> 00:35:56,904
Do you have a team?

801
00:35:56,988 --> 00:35:58,281
- Not yet.
- Do you have a plan?

802
00:35:58,364 --> 00:36:00,449
- I'd love to team up if possible.
- Should we?

803
00:36:00,533 --> 00:36:02,410
- Should we?
- The uprising of the underdogs.

804
00:36:02,493 --> 00:36:04,871
- Look at JAE JAE's and my rankings.
- I'm last.

805
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:06,831
Where are you, Stella?
You're in eighth place.

806
00:36:06,914 --> 00:36:09,417
A team where I'm the ace?
That's too much pressure.

807
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:10,918
- Come on now.
- We've only played one game so far.

808
00:36:11,002 --> 00:36:12,712
- We don't know who the real ace is yet.
- That's true.

809
00:36:12,795 --> 00:36:14,338
We'll play as a team.

810
00:36:14,422 --> 00:36:15,923
Please choose a team name.

811
00:36:16,007 --> 00:36:17,717
- How's "Jaengnuck"?
- That sounds good.

812
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:19,218
- Let's go with that.
- Sounds good.

813
00:36:19,302 --> 00:36:20,511
- You are Team Jaengnuck.
- All right.

814
00:36:20,595 --> 00:36:21,888
- We're Team Jaengnuck.
- Jaengnuck.

815
00:36:21,971 --> 00:36:23,097
Team Jaengnuck.

816
00:36:23,181 --> 00:36:27,935
HYUN KYUNG-LYUL, JANG DONG-MIN, YURISA

817
00:36:28,019 --> 00:36:30,104
- Dong-min the God.
- Yes?

818
00:36:30,188 --> 00:36:31,147
Can I join too?

819
00:36:32,815 --> 00:36:33,733
What's your plan?

820
00:36:33,816 --> 00:36:35,067
- Team or solo?
- Me?

821
00:36:35,151 --> 00:36:36,235
Team, right?

822
00:36:39,697 --> 00:36:40,948
I think…

823
00:36:41,032 --> 00:36:42,241
I'll be better off solo.

824
00:36:42,325 --> 00:36:43,743
- Solo?
- Yeah.

825
00:36:43,826 --> 00:36:48,122
Even if someone gave me the right answer,
I wouldn't trust it to be correct anyway.

826
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:52,460
I don't trust any of the 15 people here.

827
00:36:52,543 --> 00:36:55,963
And honestly, I'd be happy
to go up against all 15 of them.

828
00:36:56,881 --> 00:36:58,382
I think I need to go solo.

829
00:36:58,966 --> 00:37:00,593
Jang Dong-min,
you will play as an individual.

830
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:03,804
I think I'll go solo.
I need to see how people play first.

831
00:37:03,888 --> 00:37:04,931
Agreed.

832
00:37:05,014 --> 00:37:06,557
I wanna go solo too.

833
00:37:06,641 --> 00:37:08,893
- Yurisa, you will play as an individual.
- Yes.

834
00:37:08,976 --> 00:37:09,810
I'll go solo too.

835
00:37:09,894 --> 00:37:11,437
Hyun Kyung-lyul,
you will play as an individual.

836
00:37:11,520 --> 00:37:12,355
I'll go solo.

837
00:37:12,438 --> 00:37:13,564
Jeong Hyun-gyu,
you will play as an individual.

838
00:37:13,648 --> 00:37:15,399
This won't be easy.

839
00:37:15,483 --> 00:37:17,276
<i>Since my ranking was quite high,</i>

840
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:19,946
I wanted to team up
because I'd be fine even if my team lost.

841
00:37:20,029 --> 00:37:22,740
More solo players means
going solo would be more advantageous.

842
00:37:22,823 --> 00:37:25,034
More teams would leave the solos
at a disadvantage.

843
00:37:25,117 --> 00:37:27,495
Without multiple questions,

844
00:37:27,578 --> 00:37:30,831
teams will just be checking
each other's answers in the end.

845
00:37:30,915 --> 00:37:32,458
- Right.
- And opinions could clash.

846
00:37:32,541 --> 00:37:33,918
I'll go solo.

847
00:37:34,001 --> 00:37:35,503
XITSUH, you will play as an individual.

848
00:37:35,586 --> 00:37:36,754
I'll also go solo.

849
00:37:36,837 --> 00:37:38,297
Hong Jin-ho,
you will play as an individual.

850
00:37:38,381 --> 00:37:41,300
<i>All players</i>
<i>have completed their selections.</i>

851
00:37:41,384 --> 00:37:43,719
TEAM FORMATION

852
00:37:45,346 --> 00:37:47,348
<i>Count the Rectangles will now begin.</i>

853
00:37:47,431 --> 00:37:48,891
Round 1 will now begin.

854
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:51,811
- Wait, there are difficulty levels?
- Different difficulty levels?

855
00:37:51,894 --> 00:37:53,271
Here is the game board.

856
00:37:55,940 --> 00:37:57,358
Let's just divide and conquer.

857
00:37:58,526 --> 00:38:00,111
- Okay.
- Oh Hyun-min, Kim Dong-jae, me.

858
00:38:00,194 --> 00:38:01,112
I'll take the left.

859
00:38:11,622 --> 00:38:12,707
Jang Dong-min.

860
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:17,628
- Six.
- Six?

861
00:38:18,379 --> 00:38:19,338
Correct.

862
00:38:21,882 --> 00:38:22,717
Are you serious?

863
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:24,969
- He figured it out by looking at it.
- That was so quick.

864
00:38:25,052 --> 00:38:26,429
- What the heck?
- How did he do that?

865
00:38:26,512 --> 00:38:28,222
- Seriously?
- Did you just guess?

866
00:38:32,435 --> 00:38:33,894
Round 2 will now begin.

867
00:38:34,770 --> 00:38:36,397
Here is the game board.

868
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:37,732
What's that?

869
00:38:51,120 --> 00:38:52,163
Team Rectangle.

870
00:38:52,872 --> 00:38:53,998
Eighty-six.

871
00:38:54,081 --> 00:38:55,166
Eighty-six?

872
00:38:56,334 --> 00:38:57,418
Incorrect.

873
00:38:59,420 --> 00:39:01,088
- This is right, yeah?
- Team Gomoku.

874
00:39:01,172 --> 00:39:03,591
- Eighty-nine.
- Eighty-nine?

875
00:39:03,674 --> 00:39:05,217
- Incorrect.
- We left some out.

876
00:39:06,093 --> 00:39:07,553
- XITSUH.
- One hundred.

877
00:39:07,636 --> 00:39:09,305
One hundred? Incorrect.

878
00:39:10,890 --> 00:39:11,849
Jang Dong-min.

879
00:39:15,436 --> 00:39:16,312
One hundred fourteen.

880
00:39:16,395 --> 00:39:17,688
One hundred fourteen?

881
00:39:21,817 --> 00:39:22,693
Correct.

882
00:39:38,918 --> 00:39:43,547
THE DEVIL'S PLAN: DEAD AGAIN

883
00:39:43,631 --> 00:39:45,549
Jang Dong-min, correct.

884
00:39:47,134 --> 00:39:48,886
He really is something else.

885
00:39:48,969 --> 00:39:52,056
Jang Dong-min, you have become
a winning team with two correct answers.

886
00:39:52,139 --> 00:39:53,349
You are now exempt
from Count the Rectangles.

887
00:39:54,350 --> 00:39:56,560
Please make your way to a room.

888
00:39:57,436 --> 00:39:58,979
Maybe that spot has good energy.

889
00:40:00,606 --> 00:40:01,774
How'd he do that so quickly?

890
00:40:02,274 --> 00:40:04,568
The target number was zero,

891
00:40:04,652 --> 00:40:07,446
<i>so all I had to do</i>
<i>was calculate the empty cells.</i>

892
00:40:07,530 --> 00:40:10,241
<i>There's a formula for counting shapes.</i>

893
00:40:10,324 --> 00:40:12,326
<i>If there's a two-by-four section,</i>

894
00:40:12,410 --> 00:40:15,621
<i>you add the top two squares together,</i>

895
00:40:15,704 --> 00:40:17,039
<i>which gives you three.</i>

896
00:40:17,123 --> 00:40:19,834
<i>If you add the vertical squares,</i>
<i>you get ten.</i>

897
00:40:19,917 --> 00:40:21,502
<i>Then you multiply those two numbers,</i>

898
00:40:21,585 --> 00:40:24,839
<i>and that gives you the total number</i>
<i>of possible rectangles</i>

899
00:40:24,922 --> 00:40:27,258
<i>that can appear in that section.</i>

900
00:40:27,341 --> 00:40:28,551
<i>So you get 30 for the first one.</i>

901
00:40:28,634 --> 00:40:30,428
<i>There's another 30 in the middle.</i>

902
00:40:30,511 --> 00:40:32,888
<i>The section with 6 squares at the end</i>
<i>gives you 18.</i>

903
00:40:32,972 --> 00:40:35,141
<i>Now, for the remaining squares.</i>

904
00:40:35,224 --> 00:40:39,103
<i>You can do one times three</i>
<i>for the two-square section,</i>

905
00:40:39,186 --> 00:40:41,355
<i>but if you do that, it leaves out</i>

906
00:40:41,439 --> 00:40:44,525
<i>the overlapping rectangles you get</i>
<i>with the four-square section next to it.</i>

907
00:40:44,608 --> 00:40:47,987
So I just counted them one by one.

908
00:40:48,654 --> 00:40:50,823
- Don't worry about him.
- He's so fast.

909
00:40:50,906 --> 00:40:52,867
Round 3 will now begin.

910
00:40:52,950 --> 00:40:54,577
TARGET: 5 OR MORE

911
00:40:55,494 --> 00:40:57,246
"Or more" now?

912
00:41:01,876 --> 00:41:03,002
