00:49:46,650 --> 00:49:47,567
That's fun.

1159
00:49:47,651 --> 00:49:49,820
<i>If safety is chosen,</i>
<i>the player will lose one point</i>

1160
00:49:49,903 --> 00:49:51,822
<i>without participating in the game.</i>

1161
00:49:52,739 --> 00:49:55,117
<i>Now, the individual players</i>

1162
00:49:55,200 --> 00:49:58,161
<i>must choose either challenge or safety.</i>

1163
00:49:58,704 --> 00:50:00,539
Wait, that means
we'd be up against Dong-min.

1164
00:50:00,622 --> 00:50:02,708
- Yes.
- That's ridiculous.

1165
00:50:02,791 --> 00:50:05,127
- Only one person will participate.
- In that case…

1166
00:50:05,210 --> 00:50:07,838
- I choose challenge.
- There's no way I'm doing this.

1167
00:50:07,921 --> 00:50:12,134
I've never chosen the safe path
in my life.

1168
00:50:12,217 --> 00:50:15,846
<i>I would've chosen challenge even if</i>
<i>someone had gotten the answers before me.</i>

1169
00:50:15,929 --> 00:50:19,307
<i>Of course, there's the risk</i>
<i>of losing three points.</i>

1170
00:50:19,391 --> 00:50:22,644
But still, if you're here
on a survival show,

1171
00:50:22,728 --> 00:50:24,479
<i>wouldn't you go for challenge?</i>

1172
00:50:24,563 --> 00:50:26,481
<i>I was observing the others</i>
<i>with that in mind.</i>

1173
00:50:26,565 --> 00:50:28,984
This just really breaks your spirit.

1174
00:50:29,067 --> 00:50:30,527
Choosing safety would be the right call.

1175
00:50:30,610 --> 00:50:32,404
You're just gonna hand it to him?

1176
00:50:32,487 --> 00:50:34,156
We have no other choice. What can we do?

1177
00:50:34,656 --> 00:50:35,615
- Who would?
- Sorry?

1178
00:50:35,699 --> 00:50:37,284
- Are you gonna participate?
- Me?

1179
00:50:37,367 --> 00:50:39,077
I already made my choice.

1180
00:50:39,161 --> 00:50:44,291
I wouldn't gain points from winning,
but I would lose points if I didn't.

1181
00:50:44,374 --> 00:50:48,045
<i>I didn't see the upside,</i>
<i>so I played it safe.</i>

1182
00:50:48,128 --> 00:50:49,212
XITSUH.

1183
00:50:49,296 --> 00:50:50,672
Dong-min.

1184
00:50:51,256 --> 00:50:53,091
You wouldn't challenge yourself either.

1185
00:50:53,175 --> 00:50:55,052
- Jin-ho might do it.
- He might.

1186
00:50:55,135 --> 00:50:56,261
- Me?
- Jin-ho.

1187
00:50:56,344 --> 00:50:57,179
I gave up a while ago.

1188
00:50:57,262 --> 00:50:58,096
HONG JIN-HO: SAFETY

1189
00:50:58,180 --> 00:51:00,849
- I couldn't even win here.
- Press one.

1190
00:51:00,932 --> 00:51:01,767
I already made my choice.

1191
00:51:01,850 --> 00:51:04,686
<i>I'm naturally someone</i>
<i>who prefers challenge over comfort.</i>

1192
00:51:04,770 --> 00:51:07,898
I like to dive in headfirst.

1193
00:51:07,981 --> 00:51:12,235
But during Count the Rectangles,
I realized this isn't one of my strengths.

1194
00:51:12,319 --> 00:51:15,572
I'm already at -3 points.

1195
00:51:15,655 --> 00:51:16,656
Are you going for it?

1196
00:51:16,740 --> 00:51:17,824
You're part of a team, right?

1197
00:51:17,908 --> 00:51:20,118
- Yeah, I am, so I can't participate.
- So it doesn't affect you.

1198
00:51:20,869 --> 00:51:25,415
I mean, the players with high rankings
can afford a three-point hit,

1199
00:51:25,499 --> 00:51:27,584
- but I'm already at -3 points.
- I see.

1200
00:51:27,667 --> 00:51:30,045
So -6 points? I should just pack my bags.

1201
00:51:30,128 --> 00:51:32,631
Pieces don't matter if I'm not here.

1202
00:51:32,714 --> 00:51:35,801
<i>All players</i>
<i>have completed their selections.</i>

1203
00:51:35,884 --> 00:51:37,385
<i>Two players have chosen challenge.</i>

1204
00:51:37,469 --> 00:51:38,804
<i>Jang Dong-min</i>

1205
00:51:38,887 --> 00:51:39,930
<i>and Jeong Hyun-gyu.</i>

1206
00:51:40,972 --> 00:51:43,058
<i>The Genius </i>against <i>The Devil's Plan.</i>

1207
00:51:43,141 --> 00:51:44,351
- Showtime!
- Here we go.

1208
00:51:45,602 --> 00:51:50,398
<i>It felt like he came</i>
<i>seriously prepared this time.</i>

1209
00:51:50,482 --> 00:51:52,317
I liked that show of manliness.

1210
00:51:52,400 --> 00:51:56,321
Jang Dong-min is basically
a master of the genre,

1211
00:51:56,404 --> 00:52:00,784
<i>so I assume he has all the formulas</i>
<i>and patterns down.</i>

1212
00:52:00,867 --> 00:52:02,452
<i>But still, challenging him</i>
<i>feels like the right move.</i>

1213
00:52:02,536 --> 00:52:05,163
I just need to do well and win it.

1214
00:52:05,247 --> 00:52:06,873
- Let's have a good game.
- Sure.

1215
00:52:09,292 --> 00:52:11,086
You're a real man, Hyun-gyu.

1216
00:52:13,463 --> 00:52:15,465
<i>Count the Rectangles will now begin.</i>

1217
00:52:15,549 --> 00:52:16,383
Yes.

1218
00:52:16,466 --> 00:52:18,760
- Should we try counting too?
- Yeah, we should play.

1219
00:52:25,559 --> 00:52:27,435
Here is the game board.

1220
00:52:35,152 --> 00:52:38,488
Thirteen… Oh, there are empty squares.

1221
00:52:45,120 --> 00:52:46,121
Six?

1222
00:52:47,038 --> 00:52:48,498
- Are there more?
- At least ten.

1223
00:52:48,582 --> 00:52:49,499
Really?

1224
00:52:49,583 --> 00:52:51,084
I think eleven.

1225
00:52:51,168 --> 00:52:52,210
There are that many?

1226
00:52:53,128 --> 00:52:54,629
- Twenty-three?
- That many?

1227
00:53:02,053 --> 00:53:03,305
Jang Dong-min.

1228
00:53:03,889 --> 00:53:04,973
Twenty-seven.

1229
00:53:05,056 --> 00:53:06,308
Twenty-seven?

1230
00:53:06,391 --> 00:53:07,809
- What?
- Twenty-seven?

1231
00:53:07,893 --> 00:53:09,102
Twenty-seven?

1232
00:53:09,603 --> 00:53:10,729
Jang Dong-min…

1233
00:53:12,022 --> 00:53:12,898
correct.

1234
00:53:16,651 --> 00:53:18,320
You're on a different level.

1235
00:53:20,572 --> 00:53:23,200
- He's so quick.
- How is that even possible?

1236
00:53:23,283 --> 00:53:24,784
Good thing I didn't go for it.

1237
00:53:24,868 --> 00:53:25,744
That's just ridiculous.

1238
00:53:25,827 --> 00:53:27,078
Twenty-seven?

1239
00:53:27,579 --> 00:53:29,164
How can he be so quick?

1240
00:53:29,247 --> 00:53:32,250
<i>The game has ended</i>
<i>with Jang Dong-min's win.</i>

1241
00:53:32,334 --> 00:53:35,295
<i>He will be rewarded with three Pieces.</i>

1242
00:53:36,296 --> 00:53:37,672
That was…

1243
00:53:38,215 --> 00:53:40,133
Could you possibly spare me a Piece?

1244
00:53:40,217 --> 00:53:43,803
He really is something else.
He dominated the place in just two hours.

1245
00:53:43,887 --> 00:53:47,349
<i>Jeong Hyun-gyu was defeated</i>
<i>and will lose three points.</i>

1246
00:53:47,432 --> 00:53:48,683
Props to him for trying.

1247
00:53:50,060 --> 00:53:53,146
<i>Here are the players' current scores.</i>

1248
00:53:53,230 --> 00:53:55,023
You just need to win. That's all.

1249
00:53:55,106 --> 00:53:56,816
If you win it all like Dong-min,
you become first.

1250
00:53:56,900 --> 00:53:58,526
- Winning is the strategy.
- It is.

1251
00:53:58,610 --> 00:54:00,820
- Once your strategy is just doing well…
- Just win it all.

1252
00:54:00,904 --> 00:54:02,989
<i>We will now begin the fourth selection.</i>

1253
00:54:03,073 --> 00:54:03,990
Already?

1254
00:54:05,242 --> 00:54:07,285
<i>If the majority of players,</i>

1255
00:54:07,369 --> 00:54:10,914
<i>that is, nine or more,</i>
<i>choose greater good,</i>

1256
00:54:10,997 --> 00:54:14,376
<i>a prize token will be obtained</i>
<i>in this main match.</i>

1257
00:54:14,459 --> 00:54:18,213
<i>The said token can be used to add</i>
<i>100 million won to the prize money.</i>

1258
00:54:18,296 --> 00:54:22,592
<i>Players who choose personal gain</i>
<i>will earn five points.</i>

1259
00:54:23,551 --> 00:54:25,387
<i>- Now,</i>
- That's hilarious.

1260
00:54:25,470 --> 00:54:28,431
<i>please choose</i>
<i>either greater good or personal gain</i>

1261
00:54:28,515 --> 00:54:30,558
<i>- using the devices.</i>
<i>- </i>I'm speechless.

1262
00:54:30,642 --> 00:54:32,644
Is this how production saves
100 million won?

1263
00:54:32,727 --> 00:54:34,980
The moment the scores pop up,
you'll know who picked personal gain.

1264
00:54:35,063 --> 00:54:35,939
- Exactly.
- It's a public execution.

1265
00:54:36,022 --> 00:54:37,190
- Totally.
- Right.

1266
00:54:37,274 --> 00:54:39,484
Can everyone set aside
their personal greed

1267
00:54:39,567 --> 00:54:41,361
for the sake of the collective?

1268
00:54:41,444 --> 00:54:42,862
<i>Can they bear it for the group?</i>

1269
00:54:42,946 --> 00:54:44,072
<i>Also, can you trust them?</i>

1270
00:54:44,155 --> 00:54:46,116
<i>Do you trust</i>
<i>they will all choose the same?</i>

1271
00:54:46,199 --> 00:54:47,659
<i>It's basically a social experiment.</i>

1272
00:54:47,742 --> 00:54:50,495
Greater good is the only logical choice.

1273
00:54:50,578 --> 00:54:51,705
I'm saying this when I'm at minus points.

1274
00:54:51,788 --> 00:54:54,207
What are we even doing here?
Our prize money is zero right now.

1275
00:54:54,291 --> 00:54:55,375
Greater good.

1276
00:54:57,419 --> 00:55:00,672
If I choose greater good,
do I get the 100 million won?

1277
00:55:01,172 --> 00:55:02,549
Right, you should choose that.

1278
00:55:02,632 --> 00:55:04,801
- Winners have to choose greater good.
- There's a good chance

1279
00:55:04,884 --> 00:55:06,469
you'll walk away with it, so you should.

1280
00:55:07,095 --> 00:55:09,973
So this is our only chance
to gain a prize token today, right?

1281
00:55:10,056 --> 00:55:11,558
- Yeah, I think so.
- This is it.

1282
00:55:11,641 --> 00:55:15,437
Isn't it just best to ignore the points
that were never ours, and just choose one?

1283
00:55:15,520 --> 00:55:18,023
If we wanna go with greater good,
everyone has to be on the same page.

1284
00:55:18,106 --> 00:55:19,983
- Every single person here.
- That's true.

1285
00:55:20,066 --> 00:55:22,444
If not, then we need to choose
personal gain.

1286
00:55:22,527 --> 00:55:25,113
Does anybody here
wanna choose personal gain?

1287
00:55:25,739 --> 00:55:28,158
Those with a lot of points
would wanna go for greater good.

1288
00:55:28,241 --> 00:55:30,577
Those with less
would wanna choose personal gain.

1289
00:55:30,660 --> 00:55:33,913
But there's still a chance
of someone choosing personal gain

1290
00:55:33,997 --> 00:55:36,541
- Right, if they go rogue.
- even if we all agree on greater good.

1291
00:55:36,624 --> 00:55:38,710
Okay, then how about this?

1292
00:55:38,793 --> 00:55:41,338
Let's say we all agree on greater good,

1293
00:55:41,421 --> 00:55:43,048
but one person chooses personal gain.

1294
00:55:43,131 --> 00:55:45,216
Then, until the game ends…

1295
00:55:45,300 --> 00:55:48,094
- Exclude them?
- If they're willing to face

1296
00:55:48,178 --> 00:55:50,638
whatever comes their way on their own,
they can choose personal gain.

1297
00:55:50,722 --> 00:55:52,640
But if no one is willing
to take that risk,

1298
00:55:52,724 --> 00:55:53,767
then no one will choose it.

1299
00:55:53,850 --> 00:55:55,560
And there's another mini-game coming up.

1300
00:55:55,643 --> 00:55:57,145
- Right, there is.
- We don't know what it's gonna be.

1301
00:55:57,228 --> 00:55:58,521
- And more selections.
- That's true.

1302
00:55:58,605 --> 00:56:01,316
So we should just pretend
that those points don't exist

1303
00:56:01,399 --> 00:56:02,901
and go for greater good.

1304
00:56:02,984 --> 00:56:05,445
If there were complete freedom of choice,

1305
00:56:05,528 --> 00:56:07,364
greater good could never be the outcome.

1306
00:56:11,951 --> 00:56:13,995
You look like you're running for office
with that star.

1307
00:56:14,079 --> 00:56:14,954
Right, so…

1308
00:56:15,455 --> 00:56:17,832
- You have my support!
- You must follow my lead.

1309
00:56:17,916 --> 00:56:18,917
Oh Hyun-min has my vote!

1310
00:56:19,000 --> 00:56:20,585
I'm leaning towards greater good too.

1311
00:56:20,668 --> 00:56:23,046
Everyone here wants it,

1312
00:56:23,129 --> 00:56:25,090
but it's a trust issue.

1313
00:56:25,173 --> 00:56:27,926
You said we can punish one person
for choosing otherwise,

1314
00:56:28,009 --> 00:56:29,761
but we can't if it's, let's say,
seven people.

1315
00:56:29,844 --> 00:56:33,139
Even if it's just two people,
they could form an alliance.

1316
00:56:33,223 --> 00:56:36,184
If they have a high chance
of being eliminated regardless,

1317
00:56:36,267 --> 00:56:38,311
five points are worth more
than the potential punishment.

1318
00:56:38,395 --> 00:56:40,230
Surviving today is more important.

1319
00:56:40,313 --> 00:56:41,564
What do you think, Seok-jin?

1320
00:56:41,648 --> 00:56:42,732
- What?
- What's your take?

1321
00:56:42,816 --> 00:56:46,986
My opinion matters the least.

1322
00:56:47,070 --> 00:56:48,029
Do you have a low score?

1323
00:56:48,113 --> 00:56:50,198
- I'm at -3.
- I'm -4.

1324
00:56:50,281 --> 00:56:52,325
Right, so for us,

1325
00:56:52,409 --> 00:56:55,078
there's no reason to go for greater good

1326
00:56:55,161 --> 00:56:57,372
unless there's a guarantee
that all 16 will benefit from it.

1327
00:56:57,455 --> 00:56:59,999
<i>In situations like this,</i>
<i>I honestly wanna hold myself back.</i>

1328
00:57:00,083 --> 00:57:01,751
I just wanna stay quiet.

1329
00:57:04,087 --> 00:57:05,380
Anyone thinking of choosing greater good?

1330
00:57:05,463 --> 00:57:07,090
- I am.
- Anyone?

1331
00:57:07,173 --> 00:57:08,758
- Yes, if there's a majority.
- Me too.

1332
00:57:08,842 --> 00:57:10,969
- I choose greater good.
- I'll go for it.

1333
00:57:11,052 --> 00:57:12,887
Regardless of the results,
I'll just go for it.

1334
00:57:12,971 --> 00:57:15,515
Even if we don't have nine people,
I'll just choose it.

1335
00:57:15,598 --> 00:57:17,308
- Really?
- Yeah, really.

1336
00:57:17,392 --> 00:57:18,518
I'll do it right now.

1337
00:57:18,601 --> 00:57:19,894
- Seriously?
- I'll do it right now.

1338
00:57:20,895 --> 00:57:22,814
- I did it.
- Wait, don't.

1339
00:57:22,897 --> 00:57:23,773
Did you see it?

1340
00:57:23,857 --> 00:57:24,983
I chose option one.

1341
00:57:25,066 --> 00:57:28,987
The scores will be made public anyway.

1342
00:57:29,070 --> 00:57:31,614
So what if the rest of us
choose option two?

1343
00:57:31,698 --> 00:57:34,117
Then the real fun begins.

1344
00:57:34,701 --> 00:57:37,495
- You should've recruited two more first.
- Was it too quick?

1345
00:57:38,413 --> 00:57:43,585
I know that in the real world,
an ideal choice like this is impossible.

1346
00:57:43,668 --> 00:57:47,630
And I'm sure everyone here does too.
But this is a game.

1347
00:57:47,714 --> 00:57:51,759
So can't we live out the ideal
we've always dreamed of here?

1348
00:57:51,843 --> 00:57:53,219
Let's not overthink it.

1349
00:57:53,720 --> 00:57:55,889
I'll go for greater good too.

1350
00:57:55,972 --> 00:57:58,183
For me, 100 million won is a lot.

1351
00:57:58,266 --> 00:58:00,018
This discussion could go on forever.

1352
00:58:00,101 --> 00:58:01,853
- You're right.
- I'll just choose option one.

1353
00:58:02,479 --> 00:58:04,105
- What are you leaning towards, Yurisa?
- Sorry?

1354
00:58:04,189 --> 00:58:05,899
I'm just gonna play it by ear.

1355
00:58:06,399 --> 00:58:07,525
I'm going for option one.

1356
00:58:08,526 --> 00:58:10,236
But if we can't get nine people on board,
I'm going for two.

1357
00:58:10,320 --> 00:58:11,237
For sure.

1358
00:58:11,738 --> 00:58:14,949
We're looking for idealistic fools
to join us.

1359
00:58:15,033 --> 00:58:16,910
An idealistic fool? Sounds like me.

1360
00:58:16,993 --> 00:58:17,952
Have you made up your mind?

1361
00:58:18,036 --> 00:58:19,537
I'd love to join you.

1362
00:58:19,621 --> 00:58:22,457
- Then join us.
- But I need everyone on board first.

1363
00:58:22,540 --> 00:58:24,375
Even if this doesn't come to be,

1364
00:58:24,459 --> 00:58:28,588
I think voicing it and committing
raises the chance for others to join.

1365
00:58:28,671 --> 00:58:30,507
John Park,
we invite you to choose greater good.

1366
00:58:30,590 --> 00:58:31,925
- Option one.
- Option one!

1367
00:58:32,008 --> 00:58:34,511
- John chose option one!
- He chose option one.

1368
00:58:34,594 --> 00:58:36,346
Let's start gathering one by one.

1369
00:58:36,429 --> 00:58:38,681
- I chose option one.
- This makes me so uncomfortable.

1370
00:58:38,765 --> 00:58:40,099
Option one!

1371
00:58:40,183 --> 00:58:41,976
We're looking for idealistic fools
to join us.

1372
00:58:42,060 --> 00:58:43,436
<i>I'm definitely in favor of greater good.</i>

1373
00:58:43,520 --> 00:58:45,939
There will always be another chance
to finish first,

1374
00:58:46,022 --> 00:58:47,982
but there won't be another chance
to win this prize money.

1375
00:58:48,066 --> 00:58:49,317
This is our last chance.

1376
00:58:55,490 --> 00:58:57,784
You're worried
about losing first place, right?

1377
00:58:57,867 --> 00:58:58,868
What?

1378
00:58:58,952 --> 00:59:00,954
Your score isn't low enough
to land you in prison.

1379
00:59:02,914 --> 00:59:04,874
I'm wondering
if that's why you're conflicted

1380
00:59:04,958 --> 00:59:06,209
about choosing greater good.

1381
00:59:07,377 --> 00:59:08,419
No, it's not that.

1382
00:59:08,503 --> 00:59:10,880
I'm keeping quiet
because I'm in first place.

1383
00:59:10,964 --> 00:59:13,716
Pushing for greater good
while being in first place? I don't know.

1384
00:59:13,800 --> 00:59:15,677
You don't feel comfortable
making that statement.

1385
00:59:15,760 --> 00:59:17,428
If I do,
everyone will wanna go for personal gain.

1386
00:59:17,512 --> 00:59:19,931
- But you wanna choose greater good.
- Of course I do.

1387
00:59:20,014 --> 00:59:24,018
This is definitely a great opportunity
for those in the lower ranks

1388
00:59:24,102 --> 00:59:25,895
to turn things around.

1389
00:59:25,979 --> 00:59:28,106
But if I speak up
as someone sitting at the top,

1390
00:59:28,189 --> 00:59:31,985
<i>I'd lose my influence over others</i>
<i>in the future.</i>

1391
00:59:32,068 --> 00:59:33,945
I'll press option one.

1392
00:59:34,737 --> 00:59:35,905
- Did you press it?
- Yes.

1393
00:59:35,989 --> 00:59:36,906
That makes six, right?

1394
00:59:36,990 --> 00:59:38,908
Someone could be lying.

1395
00:59:39,450 --> 00:59:40,535
Did you lie?

1396
00:59:40,618 --> 00:59:41,452
There's a chance.

1397
00:59:41,536 --> 00:59:42,704
There's always a possibility.

1398
00:59:42,787 --> 00:59:44,998
Can everyone who hasn't chosen yet
gather over here?

1399
00:59:45,081 --> 00:59:46,874
- Who hasn't chosen yet?
- Me.

1400
00:59:48,293 --> 00:59:50,461
Why is it so hard to just press it?

1401
00:59:50,545 --> 00:59:51,963
- Oh man.
- Nobody wants to go first.

1402
00:59:52,046 --> 00:59:53,298
I really don't wanna press it.

1403
00:59:53,381 --> 00:59:54,215
Should we take a vote?

1404
00:59:54,299 --> 00:59:55,967
"If everyone agrees
to choose greater good, I will too."

1405
00:59:56,050 --> 00:59:57,885
- That's a given.
- Of course.

1406
00:59:57,969 --> 00:59:59,762
- Why wouldn't you?
- I'm not sure.

1407
00:59:59,846 --> 01:00:01,723
Even if everyone else
chooses greater good?

1408
01:00:01,806 --> 01:00:02,974
I just need some time to think.

1409
01:00:03,057 --> 01:00:04,392
Okay, sure.

1410
01:00:04,475 --> 01:00:07,520
- Five points are a lot if you rank low.
- That's totally fine.

1411
01:00:07,604 --> 01:00:11,232
If you have no choice
but to choose personal gain, that's fine.

1412
01:00:11,316 --> 01:00:14,861
We're saying we'll shut out those who say
they'll choose greater good but don't.

1413
01:00:14,944 --> 01:00:17,447
We're trying to eliminate lying.

1414
01:00:17,530 --> 01:00:18,364
That's right.

1415
01:00:18,448 --> 01:00:21,159
Even if we just get the people
who raised their hands to do it,

1416
01:00:21,242 --> 01:00:23,244
- Did you choose already?
- we'll have enough power to push through.

1417
01:00:23,328 --> 01:00:25,330
It'll be over the second I make my choice.

1418
01:00:25,413 --> 01:00:27,123
Why do you keep going on
about the wrong thing?

1419
01:00:27,206 --> 01:00:28,333
Once I do, it'll be over.

1420
01:00:28,416 --> 01:00:31,377
So if he, as the first-place player,
chooses greater good now,

1421
01:00:31,461 --> 01:00:34,005
the odds of the players below him
looking to flip things around

1422
01:00:34,088 --> 01:00:35,840
- will all choose option two.
- They'll all choose personal gain.

1423
01:00:35,923 --> 01:00:38,134
So you don't wanna lose
the first-place spot.

1424
01:00:38,217 --> 01:00:40,261
- Isn't that a given?
- That's a given for everyone.

1425
01:00:40,345 --> 01:00:43,139
- No one wants to be overtaken.
- No.

1426
01:00:43,222 --> 01:00:46,392
Wanting to avoid going to prison
and wanting to be first are different.

1427
01:00:46,476 --> 01:00:48,436
- Totally different.
- It's the same…

1428
01:00:48,519 --> 01:00:52,440
It's different
because of the alliance token.

1429
01:00:52,523 --> 01:00:54,442
To you, 100 million won

1430
01:00:54,525 --> 01:00:57,612
- matters more than first place.
- Right.

1431
01:00:57,695 --> 01:01:00,198
So you can choose option one
and push for it.

1432
01:01:00,281 --> 01:01:01,449
But a lot of people feel differently.

1433
01:01:01,532 --> 01:01:05,828
- I don't wanna lose first place.
- Right.

1434
01:01:05,912 --> 01:01:08,456
<i>This isn't an elimination game.</i>

1435
01:01:08,539 --> 01:01:10,416
So there's no reason to secure

1436
01:01:11,250 --> 01:01:12,669
the first-place position.

1437
01:01:12,752 --> 01:01:15,213
Don't get the wrong idea.

1438
01:01:15,296 --> 01:01:18,675
The reason I'm holding out is that
I want greater good to happen.

1439
01:01:18,758 --> 01:01:21,761
Then I'll go for greater good.

1440
01:01:21,844 --> 01:01:23,846
Please do. Come join us.

1441
01:01:23,930 --> 01:01:27,183
<i>I have only one goal today,</i>
<i>which is not to get eliminated.</i>

1442
01:01:27,266 --> 01:01:29,519
Also, the vibe at the time was…

1443
01:01:29,602 --> 01:01:31,646
- We already have seven people.
- Seven people made their choice?

1444
01:01:31,729 --> 01:01:33,147
Jin-ho, in last place, chose greater good.

1445
01:01:33,231 --> 01:01:34,357
So did I with six points.

1446
01:01:34,440 --> 01:01:35,274
- I was the first.
- Wait, seven?

1447
01:01:35,358 --> 01:01:38,111
If there are seven,
I'd go for personal gain.

1448
01:01:38,194 --> 01:01:39,070
You can.

1449
01:01:39,153 --> 01:01:40,988
We'll just all attack you afterward.

1450
01:01:41,072 --> 01:01:44,367
You're at six points right now, right?

1451
01:01:44,450 --> 01:01:45,910
- Yes.
- Six points.

1452
01:01:45,993 --> 01:01:49,455
- If you get five, you'll be at eleven.
- Right.

1453
01:01:49,539 --> 01:01:53,501
If you do well in the next two games,
you could even end up in first place.

1454
01:01:53,584 --> 01:01:55,545
- Right.
- If you do well.

1455
01:01:55,628 --> 01:01:59,507
But if you secure first place that way,
it'll make things difficult for you.

1456
01:02:00,258 --> 01:02:01,509
- But the thing is…
- Yeah?

1457
01:02:01,592 --> 01:02:03,094
I already pressed option two.

1458
01:02:03,177 --> 01:02:05,138
- So I can't do anything about it now.
- Oh, really?

1459
01:02:05,221 --> 01:02:08,433
My strategy was to choose personal gain
and get others to do it as well.

1460
01:02:08,516 --> 01:02:10,476
Then I can't be ostracized.

1461
01:02:10,560 --> 01:02:12,437
That's why I want you
to choose option two.

1462
01:02:13,980 --> 01:02:17,066
Kyung-lyul kept saying things
that went against the opinions

1463
01:02:17,150 --> 01:02:18,484
of the people I've been talking to.

1464
01:02:18,568 --> 01:02:22,280
<i>Which means he'll end up</i>
<i>forming an alliance opposing mine.</i>

1465
01:02:22,363 --> 01:02:25,116
And if he gets first place,
he'll use the alliance token

1466
01:02:25,199 --> 01:02:27,577
<i>to bring someone like him</i>
<i>over to his side.</i>

1467
01:02:27,660 --> 01:02:28,619
He made his choice, huh?

1468
01:02:36,461 --> 01:02:38,379
I chose personal gain.

1469
01:02:38,463 --> 01:02:40,089
- So…
- Okay.

1470
01:02:40,173 --> 01:02:42,091
So if you choose the same,
you won't be alone.

1471
01:02:42,717 --> 01:02:47,889
<i>In the past, when I lost first place,</i>

1472
01:02:47,972 --> 01:02:50,683
<i>things just got worse as time passed.</i>

1473
01:02:50,767 --> 01:02:53,603
Calling it an alliance might be a stretch,

1474
01:02:53,686 --> 01:02:57,899
<i>but I also need people</i>
<i>who can understand my viewpoint right now.</i>

1475
01:02:57,982 --> 01:03:00,860
The moment someone is alone, it's over.
Because they can just make the call.

1476
01:03:00,943 --> 01:03:04,781
It'll only work if you get all 16
to agree to it here and now.

1477
01:03:04,864 --> 01:03:05,698
Okay.

1478
01:03:06,365 --> 01:03:07,200
Come here.

1479
01:03:09,786 --> 01:03:11,287
- Me?
- Yeah.

1480
01:03:15,875 --> 01:03:19,045
- As of right now, he's…
- He's set on option two.

1481
01:03:19,128 --> 01:03:20,171
Yeah, he made his choice.

1482
01:03:20,755 --> 01:03:21,714
- Option two?
- Yeah.

1483
01:03:22,340 --> 01:03:23,758
If either of you ends up in prison,

1484
01:03:23,841 --> 01:03:26,803
I can't save you
if I'm not in the first place.

1485
01:03:26,886 --> 01:03:27,804
That's it.

1486
01:03:27,887 --> 01:03:30,431
That's why I wanna keep my first place.

1487
01:03:30,515 --> 01:03:35,770
That way, if someone I wanna work with
ends up in prison, I can save them.

1488
01:03:35,853 --> 01:03:38,898
But if he becomes first,
he definitely won't save you.

1489
01:03:40,024 --> 01:03:42,485
I'll do what I must to keep first place
and save you.

1490
01:03:44,695 --> 01:03:47,615
<i>I'm about 98% sure that their plan</i>
<i>is for one person to win</i>

1491
01:03:47,698 --> 01:03:51,202
and use the alliance token to bring back
one of the others from prison.

1492
01:03:52,411 --> 01:03:53,579
I have no other choice.

1493
01:03:53,663 --> 01:03:55,873
JANG DONG-MIN: PERSONAL GAIN

1494
01:03:55,957 --> 01:03:57,208
Did you choose?

1495
01:03:57,291 --> 01:03:59,335
- I haven't yet.
- I'm just about to.

1496
01:04:02,088 --> 01:04:02,922
Choose option two.

1497
01:04:03,005 --> 01:04:03,965
- Okay.
- Okay.

1498
01:04:04,048 --> 01:04:06,175
- There's no reason not to.
- Right.

1499
01:04:06,259 --> 01:04:07,885
- Right.
- Quite a lot of people chose option two.

1500
01:04:07,969 --> 01:04:09,846
- This is the worst case for me.
- Right.

1501
01:04:09,929 --> 01:04:11,347
I think they're going for option two.

1502
01:04:12,265 --> 01:04:16,143
I thought I might be swayed
if just one person chose personal gain.

1503
01:04:16,227 --> 01:04:18,563
And sure enough, Yi Do said…

1504
01:04:18,646 --> 01:04:20,648
I chose option two. Sorry.

1505
01:04:20,731 --> 01:04:21,983
- Okay.
- Sure.

1506
01:04:22,066 --> 01:04:23,860
But I still wasn't absolutely sure.

1507
01:04:23,943 --> 01:04:26,153
- I made my choice.
- You did?

1508
01:04:26,237 --> 01:04:27,780
- Option two?
- I had to because of my low ranking.

1509
01:04:27,864 --> 01:04:29,198
Option two? Okay.

1510
01:04:29,282 --> 01:04:33,494
If trust can't be established
and a lot of people choose option two,

1511
01:04:34,245 --> 01:04:36,205
then I can avoid becoming a public enemy.

1512
01:04:36,289 --> 01:04:38,165
Sorry. I chose option two.

1513
01:04:39,250 --> 01:04:40,501
Shindong went up.

1514
01:04:40,585 --> 01:04:44,297
<i>What others choose now</i>
<i>won't carry as much weight.</i>

1515
01:04:44,380 --> 01:04:47,884
Those who chose personal gain
justifiably needed those five points.

1516
01:04:47,967 --> 01:04:49,927
The higher-ups should decide.

1517
01:04:50,011 --> 01:04:52,889
As soon as I decide,
I'm making a sacrifice.

1518
01:04:52,972 --> 01:04:55,725
If you two are going for option one,
I'm willing to follow.

1519
01:04:55,808 --> 01:04:56,934
Should we go for option one?

1520
01:04:57,018 --> 01:04:58,769
- Let's do it.
- I won't be able to catch up.

1521
01:04:59,353 --> 01:05:00,271
I chose option one.

1522
01:05:00,354 --> 01:05:01,939
- I'll choose option one.
- You can choose option two.

1523
01:05:02,023 --> 01:05:03,149
We made an agreement.

1524
01:05:03,232 --> 01:05:04,191
I chose option one.

1525
01:05:06,444 --> 01:05:07,862
I have no choice.

1526
01:05:08,404 --> 01:05:11,574
<i>All players</i>
<i>have completed their selections.</i>

1527
01:05:11,657 --> 01:05:12,950
Show us the results.

1528
01:05:13,034 --> 01:05:15,703
It'd be pretty cool
if it's nine against seven.

1529
01:05:15,786 --> 01:05:16,621
- Nine against seven.
- Almost half.

1530
01:05:16,704 --> 01:05:18,581
Did you see it? I chose option one.

1531
01:05:18,664 --> 01:05:20,207
I'll just choose option one.

1532
01:05:20,291 --> 01:05:21,125
I did it.

1533
01:05:21,208 --> 01:05:22,585
I'm choosing one and going up.

1534
01:05:22,668 --> 01:05:24,253
John chose option one!

1535
01:05:24,962 --> 01:05:26,881
- I'll choose one as well.
- I'll choose one.

1536
01:05:26,964 --> 01:05:28,174
Then I'll go for greater good.

1537
01:05:28,257 --> 01:05:30,051
- Should we go for option one?
- Let's do it.

1538
01:05:30,134 --> 01:05:31,552
A cool nine against seven.

1539
01:05:32,053 --> 01:05:32,887
Here we go.

1540
01:05:34,013 --> 01:05:36,015
<i>Since the majority of players</i>

1541
01:05:36,098 --> 01:05:38,351
<i>did not choose greater good,</i>

1542
01:05:38,851 --> 01:05:41,479
<i>the prize token cannot be obtained.</i>

1543
01:05:42,313 --> 01:05:44,065
- We didn't get it?
- That's unbelievable.

1544
01:05:44,148 --> 01:05:46,484
Is this a prank?

1545
01:05:46,567 --> 01:05:50,237
<i>Here are the players' current scores</i>
<i>based on their selections.</i>

1546
01:05:50,321 --> 01:05:51,697
- Who was it?
- Let's see it.

1547
01:05:52,323 --> 01:05:53,950
Dong-jae.

1548
01:05:54,033 --> 01:05:55,368
- Dong-min.
- Kyung-lyul.

1549
01:05:55,451 --> 01:05:56,327
Jin-ho?

1550
01:05:56,869 --> 01:05:57,703
Jin-ho?

1551
01:05:58,871 --> 01:06:00,414
- Jin-ho?
- Jin-ho?

1552
01:06:00,498 --> 01:06:02,083
Hold on a second.

1553
01:07:41,223 --> 01:07:46,228
Subtitle translation by: Justin S. Kim
